        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): suppress unhandled stdout/stderr stream errors in execDockerRaw",
        "body": "Re-submission of #100428, which was closed automatically when the active PR queue was limited.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`execDockerRaw` attaches `data` listeners to `child.stdout` and `child.stderr`, but did not handle stream-level `error` events. A pipe read failure could therefore crash OpenClaw. Treating the error as a no-op would avoid the crash but could return success with incomplete command output.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nHandle both output streams at the shared Docker command boundary. The first stream error is retained, the Docker child receives `SIGTERM`, and the promise rejects after the child closes even when `allowFailure` is enabled. Abort status keeps precedence, and normal exit-code and Docker-not-found handling remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDocker sandbox operations no longer crash on output-pipe errors or falsely report success after output capture becomes incomplete.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression coverage emits stdout and stderr errors independently, verifies rejection, and verifies one `SIGTERM` per failed command.\n- Sanitized AWS Crabbox baseline: focused Docker tests passed 5/5 on the reviewed predecessor head (`cbx_d3efecac15bf`, `run_e27d9bec7b3c`).\n- Final AutoReview on the maintainer fixup: clean, confidence 0.90.\n- Exact-head hosted CI remains the landing gate; its only current failure is an unrelated lint regression already present on `main` in `src/channels/plugins/bundled.shape-guard.test.ts`.\n\nContributor implementation and tests remain credited to @cxbAsDev; the final lifecycle correction was added atop @vincentkoc's latest maintainer commit.\n",
        "branch": "fix/agents-sandbox-docker-stream-errors",
